--TEST--
A visibility or other modifier in front of an enum in a class body is `E0133`, and an attribute group there is accepted — `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`: an enum's cases leave the class in every
// return value, so a `private` enum would hide the name and not the values.
final class Accepted {
    #[Core\Deprecated(since: "2.0")]
    enum Status { Open, Paid }
}

final class Refused {
    private enum Status { Open, Paid }

    public static enum Kind { A, B }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0133]: an enum in a class body takes no modifier
   --> case.nvs:10:5
%A
error[E0133]: an enum in a class body takes no modifier
   --> case.nvs:12:5
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
